      "purpose": "Encrypted rollback snapshot of the current erasure saga (AES-256-GCM via the ADR-001 capability); the value is ciphertext only, and it is destroyed on commit/rollback or after the 7-day TTL. DECLARED AND WRITABLE: webSnapshotStore().write() writes this key through guardedStorage (erasureSaga/webStores.ts), so the S1 gate must keep recognizing it — an unregistered key makes the production write a silent no-op. NOT-YET-WIRED: webSnapshotStore() currently has no production caller, so no saga invokes it yet. The electron saga uses the separate erasure_snapshots entry (diskSnapshotStore under userData).",
